.TH XCALCULATOR 1 "October 2026" "Xcalculator 0.9.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xcalculator \- a calculator for Linux Mint and the Cinnamon desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xcalculator
[\-\-refresh\-rates]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Xcalculator
is a graphical calculator with Basic, Scientific, Financial, Programmer,
Unit Converter, and Currency Converter modes, chosen from its Mode menu.
.PP
The documentation is in the program itself: press F1, or choose Help \(-> Documentation.
Help \(-> Keyboard Shortcuts (Ctrl+F1) lists the shortcut keys.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-rates
Refresh the Currency Converter's exchange rates without opening a window, if they are
older than the number of days set in Preferences. It does nothing unless both
"Refresh rates automatically" and "Also when Xcalculator is closed" are switched on.
The xcalculator-rates.timer systemd user timer runs it once a day; Xcalculator switches
the timer on and off with those two settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/xcalculator/settings.json
Preferences, window sizes and the last mode used.
.TP
.I ~/.config/xcalculator/history.json
The saved history.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/xcalculator/rates.json
The exchange rates downloaded last, from the European Central Bank.
.SH AUTHOR
Wesley Hayslip.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/xlcheese/Xcalculator
